# REQUIRES: verilator
# --index-class-inputs (foldsim-index-class-inputs + fold-static): a class's
# array input read only at indices it computes -- a crossbar port arbiter's
# data_in[grant], here through two constant slices (Driver/Inputs/ports_xbar:
# the four bundles' {rdata, rvalid} into two arbiters, one class) -- becomes
# an index output and an element input per read; the simulator reads that
# element in the host cycle of the class's evaluation (the copy's index out,
# no register, back in), as the read register would hold it:
# - with --fold-ports-rows: one rows read per index and field (rdata, rvalid:
#   4 reads of 2 indices), not one per bundle; the rdata rows memory has 3
#   read ports, not 5 (the units read their own bundle's);
# - without: a choice of the frame's registers at the index, with no copy of
#   every bundle's response for the class (mp_<k>_rdata_frame_Arb).
# Spec groups (the AXI recipes' --axi-spec), SLR groups with own/env (the
# S26 recipe), bubbles, and a late-ready variant (top_late: the arbiters' ready
# from the units' late acks and the other arbiter, so each arbiter has a ready
# pass and a state pass a frame). Every run MATCHes in the host cycles of the
# build without the option (Inputs/tb_ports.sv; ports_xbar has the same ports).
# A mutant that reads the elements in reversed order MISMATCHes at cycle 4
# (checked by hand, 11-15).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/ports_xbar
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/r --static --nest --modulo --fold-ports 'mp_([0-9]+)_(.*)' --fold-ports-reset rst --fold-ports-rows --index-class-inputs Unit Arb > %t/r.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RLOG < %t/r.log
# RLOG: foldsim-index-class-inputs: Arb.data_in: 4 x 17 b read at 2 index(es), 2 instance(s)
# RLOG: indexed inputs 2 (4 rows, 0 tables, 0 choices, 0 link reads)
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=RSV < %t/r/foldsim_sim.sv
# RSV: module ports_rows_rdata_16x{{[0-9]+}}(
# RSV: R2_addr,
# RSV-NOT: R3_addr
# RSV: W0_addr,
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/r -Mdir %t/r/obj %S/Inputs/tb_ports.sv top.sv %t/r/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/r/build.log 2>&1
